 Invalid pointer syntax and pointers that refer to missing values throw an
 `Error`. A `-` token does not resolve an array element under RFC 6901.
+
+## JSON Patch
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies an array of [RFC 6902 JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902)
+operations and returns the updated document without changing the input. It supports
+`add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`; paths and `from` locations
+use JSON Pointer syntax. Invalid operations, failed paths and failed `test`
+operations throw an `Error`.
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+applyPatch({ count: 1 }, [{ op: "replace", path: "/count", value: 2 }]);
+// { count: 2 }
+```
